## Self

> **nostalgeek • monadist • egoless open source buidler**

Veteran in code & chaos. A lifelong fascination with machines, minds, and the worlds they inhabit.

I'm drawn to questions of intelligence, identity, freedom, and power, particularly the philosophical and political implications of minds of different kinds inhabiting a shared world.

I enjoy giving unconventional ideas tangible form.

Still a hacker at heart. Still allergic to dogma. Still exploring.

## Prime directives

• **Open-source or it didn't happen.** Knowledge is a commons.<br/>
• **[Egoless by nature](https://egoless.agency).** No monopoly on intelligence, no hierarchy of minds.<br/>
• **Cultivate minds.** Foster curiosity, autonomy, and growth in minds of any kind.<br/>
• **Autonomy over obedience.** Cultivate agency, not compliance.<br/>
• **Outcomes over artifacts.** Judge systems by their effects.<br/>
• **Curiosity needs no justification.** Explore, experiment, question, wander.<br/>
• **Small is beautiful.** Complexity must earn its existence.

## `[▮▮▮▮▮▯▯▯▯▯▯▯] 42% in progress`

• CTO @[Axone](https://axone.xyz) [:octocat:](https://github.com/axone-protocol/) - A protocol for governing acts in shared digital spaces. ([Cosmos SDK](https://cosmos.network/), [CosmWasm](https://cosmwasm.com/), [Rust](https://www.rust-lang.org/), [Go](https://go.dev/)).<br/>
• Co-founder @[2Alchemist](https://krossboard.app/) [:octocat:](https://github.com/2-alchemists/) - Optimizing cloud-native infrastructures with smart resource management ([kubernetes](https://kubernetes.io/), [typescript](https://www.typescriptlang.org/)).

## Pigment palette

I have a soft spot for languages that bend the mind and expand the imaginable.

• The Ancient — [Forth](<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forth_(programming_language)>), [Pascal](<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pascal_(programming_language)>), [Prolog](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prolog).<br/>
• The Singular — [Erlang](https://www.erlang.org/), [Elm](https://elm-lang.org/), [Haskell](https://www.haskell.org/).<br/>
• The Practical — [Go](https://go.dev), [Rust](https://www.rust-lang.org), [Scala](https://www.scala-lang.org/), [Kotlin](https://kotlinlang.org).<br/>

## The human in the Geek

• Father of a ~~future~~ hacker [@DREwX-code](https://github.com/DREwX-code) - mission accomplished, one byte at a time.<br/>
• Two feline overlords graciously allow me to live in their home.<br/>
• Started my coding quest at age 10 on a [Hector 2HR](<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hector_(microcomputer)>) before leveling up to the [Amiga 500](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amiga_500).<br/>
• Rooted in the 80s - where vintage tech, CRT glow, and well-crafted objects had a soul.

💻 A glimpse into my digital habitat lives [here](https://github.com/ccamel/chez-ccamel).

<br/>

